---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const updated = '14 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Fundex Global collects, uses and protects personal information submitted through this website."
  path="/privacy"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' }]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" lede={`Last updated ${updated}.`} />
  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <p>
        This policy explains how {site.legalName} ({site.name}, "we") handles personal information collected
        through this website. We aim to handle personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>

      <h2 id="collection-notice">Collection notice</h2>
      <p>
        When you use our contact form, we collect your name, email address, organisation (if you provide it), the
        type of enquiry and your message.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to read and reply to your enquiry, and to keep a record of our correspondence.</li>
        <li><strong>If you do not provide it:</strong> we cannot reply to your enquiry.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Who else sees it:</strong> service providers that help us run the website and deliver email: our
          website host (Vercel) and our email delivery provider. These providers may store data outside Australia,
          including in the United States.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Access and correction:</strong> you can ask to see or correct the information we hold about you, or
          make a complaint, as described below.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use advertising or analytics cookies and does not track you across other sites. Our host
        records standard technical information (such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested) in server
        logs to keep the site secure and working. To prevent spam, the contact form temporarily uses a one-way hash of
        your IP address and email address to limit repeated submissions.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use and keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We use enquiry information only to respond to you and to manage any resulting relationship. We do not sell
        personal information or use it for unrelated marketing. We keep enquiries only for as long as we need them for
        these purposes or as required by law, and then delete them.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        The website is served over HTTPS, and access to enquiries is limited to people who need it to respond. No
        method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so please do not send confidential or commercially
        sensitive information in a first message.
      </p>

      <h2>Access, correction and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        To ask for access to or correction of your personal information, or to make a privacy complaint, contact us
        {site.contact.emailVerified ? (<>at <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a></>) : (<>through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a></>)}.
        We will respond within a reasonable time. If
        you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner
        at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
